window.EQUITY_GAP_HELP={render:()=>"<header class=\"guide-heading\"><p class=\"kicker\">Jordan High public evidence | Cycle 1 connections</p><h1>Equity Gap Help</h1><p class=\"deck\">Learn what is behind the reports and controls, what the Jordan High evidence says, and which questions still require your own local inquiry.</p><p><a href=\"https://explorer.chrisboosalis.com\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open the separate Equity Gap App <i data-lucide=\"external-link\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1\">Cycle 1 guide</a></p></header><nav class=\"c1-contents\" aria-label=\"Equity Gap Help sections\"><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/start\">Start here</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/school\">Select school</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/report\">Full Report</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/indicators\">All Indicators</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/timeline\">Timeline</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/support\">Cycle 1 Support</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/crosswalk\">Every Cycle 1 question</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/framework\">Archived framework tutorials</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/verification\">Sources and downloads</a><a href=\"#equity-gap-help/chapter-one\">Chapter One</a></nav><article class=\"reading guide-reading c1-reading\"><section id=\"start\"><h2>Start with a question, not a conclusion</h2><p>The app organizes public school evidence. It can help you notice a pattern, compare reported groups, check counts and definitions, and prepare questions for a local investigation. It cannot tell you what a particular family experienced, whether a promised school service was usable, or why a disparity occurred.</p><p>An equity gap concerns differences in outcomes and the resources, access, and institutional commitments connected to them. Public numbers can establish an outcome pattern. Your interviews, observations, document analysis, and school commitments help you examine the opportunities behind that pattern without assuming its cause.</p><p><strong>Which evidence is real?</strong> The Jordan High values on this page come from the saved public-data evidence package. Cedar Grove, Harbor High, Canyon View, and Epsilon teaching cases are fictional and separate. Do not combine their people, counts, or findings with Jordan.</p><p class=\"source-note\">Evidence boundary: screenshots and rendered app records were saved October 6, 2026. Current local app source was inspected October 8, but production behavior and live downloads were not re-tested. Most reported outcomes here end in 2025; the capture date is not the data year. The older Framework destination shown in screenshots has been removed from current local navigation. It is explained below as archived tutorial material, not promised as a current button.</p><p>This page primarily connects the app to <strong>CalAPA Cycle 1, Parts A-D</strong>. A separate section explains how the same evidence may support a graduate <strong>Chapter One</strong>; CalAPA does not require a thesis chapter.</p></section><section id=\"school\"><h2>1. Select School: establish the identity first</h2><p>Search by school, district, county, city, or the CDS code. Select a filtered result and confirm the identity before opening a report. The stored school list can include similar names. A short list of matches is not proof that the first result is the intended school.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"School search and identity\" aria-label=\"Enlarge School search and identity\" title=\"Enlarge School search and identity\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/school.png\" alt=\"School search and identity\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>The search field narrows the list; Filtered results selects a school; Open Full Report opens the selected identity. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Control in the saved app</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th><th scope=\"col\">What appears or is retained</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Open Full Report</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Opens the report for the school you selected.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Keeps that school selected as you move through its reports. Confirm its name, district, and <a href=\"#glossary/term-cds\">CDS identifier</a>.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Filtered results</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Chooses a school from the matching results.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">The selected school identity. A similar name is not enough to establish a match.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Search by school, district, county, or city</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Narrows the school list using your search words or school identifier.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Matching schools; select and confirm one before opening its report.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Jordan example:</strong> Jordan High, Los Angeles Unified, Los Angeles County, CDS <strong>19647331934454</strong>. Older records use David Starr Jordan Senior High with the same CDS. The matching identifier, not the similar name, establishes the connection. Keep it in your working source record; protect school and person identities in submitted assessment evidence as directed.</p><p><strong>Cycle 1 connection:</strong> Part A I.1 asks you to select a student group, not merely a school. School selection makes the evidence relevant; comparing groups and explaining your choice is still your responsibility.</p><p><a href=\"sources/001_select_school_search_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Read the saved source text and tables</a></p></section><section id=\"report\"><h2>2. Full Report: see the evidence together</h2><p>Full Report combines school and reporting information, an executive summary, an indicator summary, seven detailed evidence sections, interpretation cautions, synthesis, a draft inquiry statement, a local-evidence checklist, and source verification information. Start broadly enough to notice both concerns and strengths before choosing your focal group.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Full Report and download controls\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Full Report and download controls\" title=\"Enlarge Full Report and download controls\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/report.png\" alt=\"Full Report and download controls\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>The report combines the selected school's evidence. PDF and Word controls export the report; section links move within it. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Navigation or download</th><th scope=\"col\">What is behind it</th><th scope=\"col\">How to use it</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Navigation or download\">Choose a page</td><td data-label=\"What is behind it\">Changes the app destination while retaining the selected school.</td><td data-label=\"How to use it\">Use Full Report for synthesis, All Indicators for the detailed measures, and Timeline for selected patterns over time.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Navigation or download\">Change school</td><td data-label=\"What is behind it\">Returns to school selection.</td><td data-label=\"How to use it\">Confirm the new CDS before comparing or downloading.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Navigation or download\">Report top / Back to report top</td><td data-label=\"What is behind it\">Moves to the top of the report.</td><td data-label=\"How to use it\">Return to the summary without selecting a different school.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Navigation or download\">1. Attendance; 2. ELA; 3. Math; 4. Local Conditions; 5. English Learner Progress; 6. Suspension; 7. Graduation</td><td data-label=\"What is behind it\">In-page links to the named evidence section, not seven independent data collections.</td><td data-label=\"How to use it\">Each section has its own period, population, denominator, source qualifications, and appropriate interpretation.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Navigation or download\">Download Full Report (PDF) / Download Full Report (Word)</td><td data-label=\"What is behind it\">A report document with evidence, source notes, and limitations. The local source includes academic verification tables.</td><td data-label=\"How to use it\">Retain the report as a working source, inspect the actual exported file, and select relevant evidence rather than submit the whole report as your own analysis.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>What the summary does not decide for you</h3><p>The draft inquiry statement is a starting point for thinking, not a completed Part A or B response. A low rate does not identify its cause, select the most appropriate local strategy, or establish a school's failure to meet a commitment. Look at the source tables and use the public findings to decide what to investigate locally.</p><p><a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Read the saved source text and tables</a> &middot; <a href=\"#source/report\">Read the saved report in this guide</a></p></section><section id=\"indicators\"><h2>3. All Indicators: understand each measure before using it</h2><p>All Indicators concentrates on the same seven detailed evidence sections, with tables, charts, source notes, per-table CSV downloads, and its own PDF/Word export. It does not reproduce the Full Report's entire executive-summary and synthesis narrative.</p><p>The seven app sections are not seven interchangeable CalAPA indicators. ELA and Math belong within Academic Performance. Local Conditions provides contextual evidence, while College/Career is one of the six CalAPA indicator options but is not supplied as one of these seven saved report sections. High-school DataQuest attendance is not the Dashboard TK-8 Chronic Absenteeism Indicator. Check the exact required indicator and reporting scope with the official Cycle 1 directions before selecting evidence.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"All Indicators and section navigation\" aria-label=\"Enlarge All Indicators and section navigation\" title=\"Enlarge All Indicators and section navigation\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/indicators.png\" alt=\"All Indicators and section navigation\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>The section links move to detailed evidence. Downloads retain the report's scope; a CSV is a data table, not a completed response. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><section id=\"indicator-attendance\"><h3>Indicator 1: Attendance and Engagement (Chronic Absenteeism)</h3><p>Schoolwide trend; school/district/county/state comparison; all reportable subgroup gaps; attendance reason trend and comparison.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Chronically absent students; denominator: Eligible students. Higher is more concerning.</p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> In 2024-25, 430 of 875 eligible students are reported chronically absent: 49.1%. The African American row is 100/161, or 62.1%, a 13.0 percentage-point difference above schoolwide. The English Learner attendance row is 74/181, or 40.9%. These are different groups and questions, not evidence that the graduation pattern has the same cause.</p><ul><li>DataQuest high-school attendance, not Dashboard TK-8 Chronic Absenteeism Indicator.</li><li>2020-21 DASS No is an import placeholder; later Jordan source rows say No; system references include all DASS classifications.</li><li>Reason percentages describe absence days. Average days absent divides by students with at least one absence, not all eligible students.</li><li>No student-level or causal link between absence and achievement is established.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Attendance available-year trend\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Attendance available-year trend\" title=\"Enlarge Attendance available-year trend\"><img src=\"assets/attendance-trend.png\" alt=\"Attendance available-year trend\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Attendance subgroup differences\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Attendance subgroup differences\" title=\"Enlarge Attendance subgroup differences\"><img src=\"assets/attendance-gaps.png\" alt=\"Attendance subgroup differences\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"713\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Academic year</th><th scope=\"col\">Chronically absent / eligible</th><th scope=\"col\">Reported rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2020-21</td><td data-label=\"Chronically absent / eligible\">359 / 865</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">41.5%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2021-22</td><td data-label=\"Chronically absent / eligible\">462 / 841</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">54.9%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2022-23</td><td data-label=\"Chronically absent / eligible\">410 / 873</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">47%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2023-24</td><td data-label=\"Chronically absent / eligible\">424 / 934</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">45.4%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2024-25</td><td data-label=\"Chronically absent / eligible\">430 / 875</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">49.1%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.2, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.1, B.2, B.4, B.5, C.1, C.2. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-ela\"><h3>Indicator 2: Smarter Balanced ELA</h3><p>Schoolwide available-year trend, system comparison, primary subgroup gaps, additional audit/reference subgroup rows, official results link.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Source-reported met/exceeded count when present; unavailable in older retained layouts; denominator: Valid scores. Higher is more favorable.</p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> The 2024-25 Jordan ELA result is 55.28% meeting or exceeding standard, with 123 valid scores, 123 tested, and 126 enrolled in the retained record. Use the source-reported combined percentage; rounded performance-level components can sum differently. This is Smarter Balanced percent met/exceeded, not Dashboard Distance from Standard.</p><ul><li>Smarter Balanced percent met/exceeded, not DFS; CAA excluded.</li><li>Aggregate grade code 13 means all tested grades, not grade 13. Saved latest Jordan underlying grade is Grade 11.</li><li>Enrolled, tested and valid scores differ; do not substitute one denominator for another.</li><li>At least 11 valid scores required by displayed primary filter; 11-29 need small-group caution.</li><li>Primary and audit/reference subgroup rows must stay separate.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"ELA percent met or exceeded\" aria-label=\"Enlarge ELA percent met or exceeded\" title=\"Enlarge ELA percent met or exceeded\"><img src=\"assets/ela-trend.png\" alt=\"ELA percent met or exceeded\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Academic year</th><th scope=\"col\">Source percent met/exceeded</th><th scope=\"col\">Tested / valid scores / enrolled</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2020-21</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">38.14%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">103 / 97 / 185</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2021-22</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">18.95%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">153 / 153 / 169</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2022-23</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">30.68%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">176 / 176 / 187</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2023-24</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">26.4%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">178 / 178 / 179</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2024-25</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">55.28%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">123 / 123 / 126</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Grade code 13 in this aggregate record means all tested grades, not Grade 13. Jordan's latest underlying tested grade is Grade 11; all-grade district and state figures are not automatically grade-matched comparisons. Do not reconstruct unavailable older numerators from rounded percentages.</p><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.5, C.2. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-math\"><h3>Indicator 3: Smarter Balanced Math</h3><p>Same academic controls and views as ELA, with separately qualified Math results.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Source-reported met/exceeded count when present; unavailable in older retained layouts; denominator: Valid scores. Higher is more favorable.</p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> The 2024-25 Math result is 24.79% meeting or exceeding standard, with 121 valid scores, 121 tested, and 126 enrolled. Do not reuse ELA's 123 denominator. The difference between subject rates suggests questions about learning opportunities, but it does not establish the effect of a particular teacher or program.</p><ul><li>Same measure/grade/valid-score restrictions as ELA.</li><li>Math 2025 denominator is 121, not ELA&#x27;s 123 or enrolled 126.</li><li>No academic subgroup Timeline Explorer capability is evidenced.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Math percent met or exceeded\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Math percent met or exceeded\" title=\"Enlarge Math percent met or exceeded\"><img src=\"assets/math-trend.png\" alt=\"Math percent met or exceeded\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Academic year</th><th scope=\"col\">Source percent met/exceeded</th><th scope=\"col\">Tested / valid scores / enrolled</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2020-21</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">9.47%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">96 / 95 / 185</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2021-22</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">3.23%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">155 / 155 / 170</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2022-23</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">3.41%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">176 / 176 / 186</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2023-24</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">6.21%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">177 / 177 / 179</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Academic year\">2024-25</td><td data-label=\"Source percent met/exceeded\">24.79%</td><td data-label=\"Tested / valid scores / enrolled\">121 / 121 / 126</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>Grade code 13 in this aggregate record means all tested grades, not Grade 13. Jordan's latest underlying tested grade is Grade 11; all-grade district and state figures are not automatically grade-matched comparisons. Do not reconstruct unavailable older numerators from rounded percentages.</p><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.5, C.2. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-local\"><h3>Indicator 4: Local Conditions and System Context</h3><p>LEA priorities 1 Basic Services and Conditions; 2 Implementation of State Academic Standards; 3 Parent and Family Engagement; 6 School Climate; 7 Access to a Broad Course of Study. Priority-specific inquiry/evidence prompts; Historical Not Met Records; source-file details.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Not applicable to this context measure; denominator: Not applicable to this context measure. </p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> The five loaded 2025 LAUSD local priorities are reported Met, with a June 24, 2025 board date. This concerns reporting and measurement standards. It does not certify that every Jordan student had equitable access, that climate was favorable, or that a specific support was implemented.</p><ul><li>All five 2025 LAUSD priorities shown as Met, board meeting 2025-06-24; Pr12025.txt, Pr22025.txt, Pr32025.txt, Pr62025.txt, Pr72025.txt.</li><li>Met refers to annual measurement/reporting standards, not proof of equitable outcomes or implementation at Jordan.</li><li>Historical Not Met section says none found in loaded records; not proof no local need exists.</li></ul><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Local priority</th><th scope=\"col\">Question the context suggests</th><th scope=\"col\">Local evidence still needed</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Local priority\">1: Basic services</td><td data-label=\"Question the context suggests\">Are the promised people, materials, and facilities available and usable?</td><td data-label=\"Local evidence still needed\">Staff allocations, materials access, facilities records, and relevant experiences.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Local priority\">2: State standards</td><td data-label=\"Question the context suggests\">Who has access to the intended curriculum and instruction?</td><td data-label=\"Local evidence still needed\">Course and lesson evidence, supports, and implementation records.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Local priority\">3: Family engagement</td><td data-label=\"Question the context suggests\">Can families participate meaningfully and obtain a response?</td><td data-label=\"Local evidence still needed\">Accessible communications, family perspectives, response processes.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Local priority\">6: School climate</td><td data-label=\"Question the context suggests\">Whose experiences are represented in the climate evidence?</td><td data-label=\"Local evidence still needed\">Local climate instruments, participation, interviews or observations.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Local priority\">7: Broad course of study</td><td data-label=\"Question the context suggests\">Who can enroll and participate in needed courses?</td><td data-label=\"Local evidence still needed\">Schedules, prerequisites, enrollment and advising processes.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.III.1, A.IV.2, A.IV.4, A.IV.5, B.1, B.2, B.3, B.4, C.1, C.3, C.5. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-elpi\"><h3>Indicator 5: English Learner Progress and Language Access: Jordan High</h3><p>Acronym guide; Census Day EL/FEP trend; home languages; LTEL/At-Risk grade context; ELPI status, counts, participation additions, change/color and historical qualification tables.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> ELPI progress-criteria count; denominator: ELPI source accountability denominator, including source-year participation additions. </p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> Jordan's 2025 ELPI record reports 70/126, or 55.6%, meeting the progress criteria, with a current participation addition of zero in this source year. The 126 is an accountability denominator, not the Census Day count of English learners. Its complement is not a simple estimate of all English learners who failed.</p><ul><li>Census counts are not the ELPI denominator, total school enrollment, or annual reclassification counts.</li><li>EL/FEP/RFEP/LTEL/duration fields are not interchangeable and can overlap.</li><li>DataQuest LTEL and Dashboard LTEL use different definitions and populations.</li><li>Historical 2019/2022 participation additions not reported; do not assume zero. 2023 Jordan prior additions 8.</li><li>2025 LTEL change is source-reported +43.8 points; do not replace with subtraction of rounded 72.9 and 29.2.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"English Learner Progress available-year trend\" aria-label=\"Enlarge English Learner Progress available-year trend\" title=\"Enlarge English Learner Progress available-year trend\"><img src=\"assets/elpi-trend.png\" alt=\"English Learner Progress available-year trend\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Reporting year</th><th scope=\"col\">Progress count / denominator</th><th scope=\"col\">Reported rate and qualification</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2019</td><td data-label=\"Progress count / denominator\">24 / 122</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate and qualification\">19.7%; Historical EL aggregate; no student-group field. Participation adjustment not reported; do not assume zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2022</td><td data-label=\"Progress count / denominator\">44 / 116</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate and qualification\">37.9%; Historical EL aggregate; no student-group field. Participation adjustment not reported; do not assume zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2023</td><td data-label=\"Progress count / denominator\">43 / 128</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate and qualification\">33.6%; Historical EL aggregate; no student-group field. Current participation addition 0; prior addition 8. Verify source-year rules.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2024</td><td data-label=\"Progress count / denominator\">42 / 145</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate and qualification\">29%; Reported accountability denominator. Current participation addition 0; verify source-year rules.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2025</td><td data-label=\"Progress count / denominator\">70 / 126</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate and qualification\">55.6%; Reported accountability denominator. Current participation addition 0; verify source-year rules.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.2, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.1, B.2, B.4, B.5, C.1, C.5. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-suspension\"><h3>Indicator 6: Suspension and Discipline Equity</h3><p>Suspension trend, district/state comparison, subgroup gaps, status/change/color/source qualifications; expulsion trend and school/district/county/state context.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Suspended students / expelled students; total expulsions also separately reported; denominator: Source cumulative enrollment, specific to measure and entity. </p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> The 2025 record reports 0 suspended students in a cumulative enrollment of 940, a 0.0% suspension rate. This is a reported strength to examine alongside student experience; it is not proof that every disciplinary experience was equitable or that no informal removal occurred. Expulsions use their own records and populations.</p><ul><li>Zero reported suspension is not proof of fair experiences or zero informal removals.</li><li>Not certified/data-error records must not become ordinary zero values.</li><li>District suspension denominator 388896 differs from expulsion 537536 and attendance 528612; keep source populations.</li><li>No county suspension line in Timeline Explorer; expulsion county comparison is a different measure.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Suspension reference comparison\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Suspension reference comparison\" title=\"Enlarge Suspension reference comparison\"><img src=\"assets/suspension-comparison.png\" alt=\"Suspension reference comparison\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">2025 entity</th><th scope=\"col\">Suspended / cumulative enrollment</th><th scope=\"col\">Reported rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">Jordan High</td><td data-label=\"Suspended / cumulative enrollment\">0 / 940</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">0%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">Los Angeles Unified</td><td data-label=\"Suspended / cumulative enrollment\">1343 / 388896</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">0.3%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">California</td><td data-label=\"Suspended / cumulative enrollment\">170274 / 5961200</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">2.9%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.2, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.1, B.2, B.4, B.5, C.1. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><section id=\"indicator-graduation\"><h3>Indicator 7: Graduation and Completion Evidence</h3><p>Schoolwide trend, district/state comparison, subgroup gaps, graduates/accountability denominator, fifth-year graduates, measure definition, status/change/color.</p><p><strong>Read the measure:</strong> Graduates under source-year accountability definition; denominator: Dashboard denominator; field named cohort_students in stored evidence is not automatically a four-year-only cohort. </p><p><strong>Real Jordan example:</strong> In 2025, Jordan reports 170 graduates against an accountability denominator of 198, or 85.9%. The English Learner row is 46/65, or 70.8%, 15.1 percentage points below schoolwide. Schoolwide improvement can coexist with a persistent subgroup difference.</p><ul><li>2024/2025 combined four-/five-year measure adds prior-class fifth-year graduates, not all fifth-year students, to the current cohort denominator.</li><li>2021-2023 retain explicit historical-measure/DASS variant verification warning.</li><li>No county graduation line in Timeline Explorer.</li><li>Subgroup below schoolwide is a percentage-point comparison; schoolwide includes subgroup, not an independent comparison group.</li></ul><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Graduation available-year trend\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Graduation available-year trend\" title=\"Enlarge Graduation available-year trend\"><img src=\"assets/graduation-trend.png\" alt=\"Graduation available-year trend\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Graduation reference comparison\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Graduation reference comparison\" title=\"Enlarge Graduation reference comparison\"><img src=\"assets/graduation-comparison.png\" alt=\"Graduation reference comparison\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"700\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Graduation subgroup differences\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Graduation subgroup differences\" title=\"Enlarge Graduation subgroup differences\"><img src=\"assets/graduation-gaps.png\" alt=\"Graduation subgroup differences\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1200\" height=\"521\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Jordan High public-data chart, prepared October 6 from the source app's evidence and renderer. Read the nearby measure cautions and source table; this is not a live chart.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">2025 entity</th><th scope=\"col\">Graduates / accountability denominator</th><th scope=\"col\">Reported rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">Jordan High</td><td data-label=\"Graduates / accountability denominator\">170 / 198</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">85.9%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">Los Angeles Unified</td><td data-label=\"Graduates / accountability denominator\">25851 / 29899</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">86.5%</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"2025 entity\">California</td><td data-label=\"Graduates / accountability denominator\">445720 / 507889</td><td data-label=\"Reported rate\">87.8%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The 2024/2025 measure combines four- and five-year graduation evidence under the source definition. The fifth-year addition is prior-class fifth-year graduates, not every fifth-year student. The stored field named cohort_students must not be relabeled a four-year-only cohort. Historical 2021-2023 definitions and DASS variants require checking before treating the full line as an unchanged measure.</p><p><strong>Cycle 1 use:</strong> A.I.1, A.IV.1, A.IV.3, A.IV.4, B.1, B.4, B.5, C.1, C.2. <a href=\"sources/010_full_report_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Inspect the original report tables and qualifications</a>.</p></section><h3>What each table-download button contains</h3><p>The following labels appear in the saved Full Report and All Indicators. A CSV retains a table for your own inspection; it does not transfer a chart's qualifications automatically into your writing. Keep the source notes with it.</p><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">CSV control</th><th scope=\"col\">Table behind it</th><th scope=\"col\">Interpretation to retain</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download available-year trend table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Available-year trend table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download system comparison table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">System comparison table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download chronic absenteeism subgroup table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Chronic absenteeism subgroup table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare reported group rows, their counts, and the named reference. Categories may overlap; suppressed values are not zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download attendance reason trend as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Attendance reason trend</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Absence-reason evidence concerns days; it is not a percentage of students who report a reason.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download attendance reason comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Attendance reason comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Absence-reason evidence concerns days; it is not a percentage of students who report a reason.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download ELA trend table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Ela trend table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download ELA system comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Ela system comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download ELA subgroup gap table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Ela subgroup gap table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare reported group rows, their counts, and the named reference. Categories may overlap; suppressed values are not zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download Math trend table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Math trend table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download Math system comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Math system comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download Math subgroup gap table as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Math subgroup gap table</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare reported group rows, their counts, and the named reference. Categories may overlap; suppressed values are not zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download Local Indicators context lenses as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Local indicators context lenses</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Context for inquiry, not proof of local implementation or student experience.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download English learner context trend as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">English learner context trend</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download source-qualified LTEL context as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Source-qualified ltel context</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Retains available source qualifications with the selected measure. Keep the group definition and source-year denominator notes.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download source-qualified ELPI as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Source-qualified elpi</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Retains available source qualifications with the selected measure. Keep the group definition and source-year denominator notes.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download suspension trend as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Suspension trend</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download suspension comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Suspension comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download suspension subgroup gaps as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Suspension subgroup gaps</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare reported group rows, their counts, and the named reference. Categories may overlap; suppressed values are not zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download expulsion trend as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Expulsion trend</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download expulsion comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Expulsion comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download graduation trend as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Graduation trend</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Examine available years with their source populations. Missing years are not zero and annual rows do not track identical students.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download graduation comparison as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Graduation comparison</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare the named entities for the reported period. Reference populations are not matched control groups.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"CSV control\">Download graduation subgroup gaps as CSV</td><td data-label=\"Table behind it\">Graduation subgroup gaps</td><td data-label=\"Interpretation to retain\">Compare reported group rows, their counts, and the named reference. Categories may overlap; suppressed values are not zero.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><strong>Download All Indicators (PDF)</strong> and <strong>Download All Indicators (Word)</strong> provide the indicator-focused document, not a different dataset. <a href=\"sources/020_all_indicators_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Read the saved source text and tables</a>.</p></section><section id=\"timeline\"><h2>4. Equity Timeline Explorer: compare patterns across available years</h2><p>Choose the indicator first, then the primary student group and appropriate reference lines. The available choices depend on the measure. A selectable group does not guarantee a reportable value in every year.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Timeline with English Learner graduation selected\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Timeline with English Learner graduation selected\" title=\"Enlarge Timeline with English Learner graduation selected\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/timeline.png\" alt=\"Timeline with English Learner graduation selected\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>This saved screenshot shows Graduation and English Learners. The separately saved graduation text view uses African American / Black; do not attribute one selection's values to the other. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Control in the saved app</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th><th scope=\"col\">What appears or is retained</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download Equity Timeline Explorer (PDF)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the timeline chart, selected evidence, and source cautions. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download Equity Timeline Explorer (Word)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the timeline chart, selected evidence, and source cautions. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download Timeline Data (CSV)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads the selected timeline records as a spreadsheet-readable table.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Years, named lines, values, group codes, counts, and available source qualifications. Missing values may remain in these records.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download source-qualified timeline evidence as CSV</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads the records used to draw the selected timeline.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">The same source fields after rows without a year, named line, or value are excluded. It can contain fewer rows than the main timeline CSV; a missing value is not zero.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Indicator</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Chooses the measure to explore over time.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">The group choices, reference lines, chart, and evidence table update for that measure.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Group category</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Narrows the attendance group choices.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">For example, race/ethnicity or high-interest student groups. Availability depends on the saved measure.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Primary group</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Chooses the school student group to follow.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Its available years, values, counts, and source notes. A listed group may lack a reportable value in some years.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">All Students</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">District: All Students</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">County: All Students</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">State: All Students</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">District: Same Group</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">State: Same Group</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Shows or hides the named reference line.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Compare that population with the primary group. All Students includes many learners outside the selected group; Same Group follows the ELPI group definition for that source year.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>What changes when you change a control?</h3><p><strong>Indicator</strong> offers Chronic Absenteeism, Suspension, Graduation, and ELPI in the saved explorer. It does not offer ELA or Math subgroup timelines. Academic schoolwide trends are available in the report. <strong>Group category</strong> narrows attendance choices; <strong>Primary group</strong> chooses the school subgroup series.</p><p>For attendance, the reference checkboxes can include school, district, county, and state All Students. Suspension and graduation use school, district, and state All Students, not county suspension or matched district subgroups. ELPI instead uses <strong>District: Same Group</strong> and <strong>State: Same Group</strong>, with EL or LTEL definitions appropriate to that source. There is no schoolwide All Students ELPI reference.</p><h3>Read below the line chart</h3><p>The <strong>Context</strong> identifies the school and measure. <strong>Selectable lines</strong> explains the chosen series. The <strong>Readable Evidence Table</strong> presents the observations, and <strong>Counts, Denominators, and Source Group Codes</strong> helps you inspect who and what each rate represents. The two CSV download positions use the selected source-qualified timeline data. A PDF/Word download preserves the page report. Keep the source qualifications even when a chart appears simple.</p><h3>Three-year Jordan graduation example for Part A</h3><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Reporting year</th><th scope=\"col\">English Learners</th><th scope=\"col\">Schoolwide</th><th scope=\"col\">EL minus schoolwide</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2023</td><td data-label=\"English Learners\">36/52; 69.2%</td><td data-label=\"Schoolwide\">78.1%</td><td data-label=\"EL minus schoolwide\">-8.9 percentage points</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2024</td><td data-label=\"English Learners\">31/47; 66%</td><td data-label=\"Schoolwide\">81.2%</td><td data-label=\"EL minus schoolwide\">-15.2 percentage points</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Reporting year\">2025</td><td data-label=\"English Learners\">46/65; 70.8%</td><td data-label=\"Schoolwide\">85.9%</td><td data-label=\"EL minus schoolwide\">-15.1 percentage points</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The reported EL rate falls from 69.2% to 66.0%, then rises to 70.8%; schoolwide rises from 78.1% to 85.9%. The selected-group difference is present in all three reported years. This supports investigating the pattern, while the source-year graduation-definition change limits a simple like-for-like trend interpretation. It does not identify which students lacked a service or what caused the difference.</p><p>For the 2025 difference, 70.8 minus 85.9 equals -15.1 <strong>percentage points</strong>, not a 15.1% relative reduction or a count of students. The schoolwide group includes English learners, so these are not independent populations. A larger reference group is not a control group.</p><p><a href=\"sources/graduation_el_history.csv\" download>Saved EL graduation history CSV</a> &middot; <a href=\"sources/050_timeline_default_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Saved attendance Timeline view</a> &middot; <a href=\"sources/052_timeline_graduation_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Saved graduation Timeline view: African American / Black</a></p></section><section id=\"support\"><h2>5. CalAPA Cycle 1 Support: turn public evidence into an inquiry</h2><p>This destination explains evidence requirements, selected-school coverage, rubric alignment, readiness, quantitative and qualitative evidence, school commitments, focus selection, educational partners, and submission/privacy boundaries. Its Leadership Inquiry Alignment Guide, Claim Strength Guide, and Do / Do Not Claim comparisons help you check the reasoning between a number and a proposed action.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"CalAPA Cycle 1 Support\" aria-label=\"Enlarge CalAPA Cycle 1 Support\" title=\"Enlarge CalAPA Cycle 1 Support\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/support.png\" alt=\"CalAPA Cycle 1 Support\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>The support page organizes the work still needed. It is not a scoring tool, response editor, or certification of a completed submission. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Control in the saved app</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th><th scope=\"col\">What appears or is retained</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download CalAPA Cycle 1 Support (PDF)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the Cycle 1 inquiry guidance and evidence-readiness explanations. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download CalAPA Cycle 1 Support (Word)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the Cycle 1 inquiry guidance and evidence-readiness explanations. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A coverage or readiness table can tell you that data are loaded. It cannot certify that you selected an appropriate group, analyzed three qualitative sources, obtained authentic leadership feedback, or met a rubric. The PDF and Word buttons export support guidance, not your own CalAPA response.</p><h3>From a public pattern to a local question</h3><p>The reported 2025 EL graduation result suggests asking how students obtain the courses, advice, and timely support needed for completion. It does not establish that advising was absent or inaccessible at Jordan. Those are questions for local evidence. Examine verified allocations and commitments, ask about specific experiences of seeking help, and look for successful cases as well as barriers.</p><p>For example, a local inquiry could compare student accounts of requesting support, observations of an advising process, and document evidence of referral follow-through. These are proposed source types, not collected Jordan findings. Three quotations from one interview do not become three different qualitative sources.</p><p><a href=\"sources/030_calapa_cycle1_support_jordan_high.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Read the saved source text and tables</a></p></section><section id=\"crosswalk\"><h2>Every Cycle 1 question: what the app contributes and what you supply</h2><p>The prompts below are linked to the full Cycle 1 teaching explanation. Public evidence is most directly useful in Part A. In Parts B-D it helps sustain the reasoning, but cannot replace local investigation, research, feedback, your decisions, or reflection.</p><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-i-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | direct quantitative support</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q1\">A.I.1</a>: Identify the one specific student group you have chosen to further investigate.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Select a defensible group after comparing all available outcomes and denominators.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> English Learner graduation is 46/65, 70.8%, versus schoolwide 170/198, 85.9%, in 2025; African American attendance is 100/161, 62.1%, versus 430/875, 49.1%, in 2024-25.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Candidate selects and justifies one group and checks recent related evidence. Do not let the app&#x27;s lead example automatically choose it.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-24\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: interpreting the pattern</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q1\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 TABLE 3,8,12,23; 050-053; 030 MARKDOWN 24,29</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iii-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | orientation only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q2\">A.III.1</a>: Investigate the vision, mission, and/or goals at your school and document your findings.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use school identity and local-priority prompts to locate relevant official school documents.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Jordan CDS 19647331934454 identifies the school; LAUSD Met statuses are district context.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Obtain and document the school&#x27;s actual vision/mission/goals and dates; no school mission text is supplied by these reports.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-9\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: interpreting the pattern</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q2\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>001; 010 Local Conditions; 030 MARKDOWN 9</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iv-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | direct quantitative support</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q3\">A.IV.1</a>: Reflecting upon the data collected and analyzed, what supports your decision to select this specific equity gap for your identified group of students? Share your analysis for the specific quantitative data you included in Section II of the Data Collection and Equity Gap Analysis template and your rationale for collecting it. How are these data relevant to understanding equity issues at the school for student groups?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use recent related quantitative years, same-year subgroup/schoolwide gaps, context and evidence qualifications to justify selection.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> EL graduation: 2023 36/52=69.2%, 2024 31/47=66.0%, 2025 46/65=70.8%; schoolwide 78.1%,81.2%,85.9%; gaps -8.9,-15.2,-15.1 points.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Explain rationale using actual local qualitative analysis too. Preserve historical graduation definitions. Template IV.1 itself says quantitative data in Section II although the table is in Section I; do not silently rewrite the original prompt.</p><p><a href=\"#source/report/table-23\">Saved Full Report: graduation evidence table</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q3\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 TABLE 1-23; 030 TABLE 1; 050-053; evidence.js graduation_el_history</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iv-2\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | planning support only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q4\">A.IV.2</a>: Describe the three different qualitative data sources you included in Section II of the Data Collection and Equity Gap Analysis template. How did these sources provide more information about this student group for the California state indicator?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use local-evidence checklist and framework examples to plan relevant qualitative sources.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> For EL completion, reports suggest transcript/counseling/ELD records and student/family perspectives, but do not supply those records or accounts.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Collect/analyze three real qualitative sources and explain each contribution. Public numerical tables are not three qualitative sources.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-10\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: interpreting the pattern</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q4\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 Leadership Inquiry Local Evidence Checklist; 030 MARKDOWN 10-12,22-23; 041 data collection; 043 qualitative strand</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iv-3\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | quantitative plus optional integration guidance</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q5\">A.IV.3</a>: What patterns and/or trends related to the California state indicator and student group equity issues did you find in the qualitative data? How do they relate to the quantitative data patterns and/or trends you identified?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Pair a verified public pattern with actual qualitative themes; use High School tutorial&#x27;s integration distinctions to examine agreement and disagreement.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> EL graduation improves 66.0% to 70.8% while remaining 15.1 points below schoolwide in 2025. This is the quantitative side only.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Supply genuine themes, quotations/artifacts and a reasoned relationship; do not manufacture confirming interviews or student-level links.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-12\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: interpreting the pattern</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q5\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>050-053 TABLE 1-2; 043 sections 9-10; 030 MARKDOWN 12,22</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iv-4\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | partial evidence and reasoning support</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q6\">A.IV.4</a>: Define the equity gap you identified for a student group through your quantitative and qualitative data analyses. Discuss related research and explain how this research informs and/or supports your equity gap analysis finding for the California state indicator and student group you identified.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use exact measure/group/year/gap, analyze local conditions, and connect relevant scholarship from reviewed sources.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> 2025 EL graduation gap is -15.1 percentage points, not 15.1 percent fewer students or proof of inadequate ELD.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Integrate local qualitative evidence and actually read/cite relevant research in the response. Epsilon findings are synthetic and references are not automatically evidence of Jordan causes.</p><p><a href=\"#source/report/table-23\">Saved Full Report: graduation evidence table</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q6\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 synthesis/guardrails; 030 claim guide; 040-044 theory-to-evidence tutorials and references</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-a-iv-5\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part A | orientation only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q7\">A.IV.5</a>: How is the equity gap you identified for a student group at your school related to specific components of the school&#x27;s vision, mission, and/or goals?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Carry the defined gap into a documented school-goal comparison.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> EL completion rates can be compared to an actual locally documented completion/equity goal, once obtained.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Identify exact school-goal components and explain the relationship; the app supplies neither that goal nor the completed alignment.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-9\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: interpreting the pattern</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/a-q7\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>030 MARKDOWN 9; 010 Local Conditions and synthesis</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-b-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part B | inquiry scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q1\">B.1</a>: What potential contributing factors are suggested by the data you have collected and analyzed that may have created or added to the equity gap you identified for a student group at your school?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Convert outcome patterns into testable local questions using conditions, access and implementation prompts.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> EL graduation gap suggests examining course access, counseling, ELD scheduling, credit recovery and student/family experience; none is established as a cause.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Identify plausible factors supported by candidate-collected evidence; distinguish hypothesis from finding.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-13\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: investigating contributing conditions</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q1\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 Local Conditions, English Learner context, local evidence checklist; 030 MARKDOWN 13-15; 040,043</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-b-2\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part B | reasoning scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q2\">B.2</a>: How do these specific contributing factors, including institutional and/or structural factors, impact student learning or well-being for the student group?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use framework distinction between documented availability and experienced accessibility to investigate mechanisms.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> A course may be listed as available while access is unverified; Jordan&#x27;s rate alone cannot show the pathway to outcomes.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Explain factors&#x27; impact with local evidence and research; do not claim tutoring permissions or school scheduling caused Jordan results.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: inquiry and claim guidance</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q2\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 priority-specific prompts; 040 conceptual framework; 043 sections 4,7-10</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-b-3\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part B | research orientation only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q3\">B.3</a>: Cite research related to your findings regarding contributing factors that may have created or added to the equity gap you have identified for the student group.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Framework reference lists and theory arguments suggest scholarship to examine.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Community Cultural Wealth and culturally responsive leadership can guide non-deficit questions; neither proves a local mechanism.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Read and select research that matches the actual finding; embed citations in original response as template directs. Bibliographic links were not network-verified.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-15\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: investigating contributing conditions</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q3\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>040 References and theory sections; 041-044 References; 030 MARKDOWN 15</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-b-4\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part B | inquiry scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q4\">B.4</a>: Identify areas of educational need related to the single equity gap for a group of students (e.g., the school needs additional supports or materials, necessary specialists or counselors, after-school programs for students).</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use outcome and access evidence prompts to identify a bounded need rather than jump to a generic intervention.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> EL 46/65 graduation is an outcome signal; it does not itself demonstrate a counselor staffing shortage.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Determine and substantiate one related need from local resources, experiences and implementation evidence.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: inquiry and claim guidance</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q4\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 graduation/EL context/Local Conditions; 030 readiness and claim guidance</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-b-5\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part B | partial descriptive evidence</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q5\">B.5</a>: Problem Statement: Describe the equity gap that needs to be addressed at the chosen school for the California state indicator and the identified student group&#x27;s area of need (achievement and/or well-being).</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use the source-bound group/measure/year statement and add the locally substantiated need.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Jordan 2025 EL graduation 70.8% (46/65) versus 85.9% (170/198), -15.1 points, under the combined accountability measure.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Author the specific problem statement; do not copy an app-generated draft or infer unobserved causes.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-13\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: investigating contributing conditions</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/b-q5\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 draft inquiry statement and TABLE 23; 030 MARKDOWN 13-15,29-31</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-c-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part C | planning scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q1\">C.1</a>: For the student equity gap you identified in Step 1, describe the potential strategies you identified for equitable school improvement and how they are to be applied.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Evidence and local-condition prompts help align possible action to the selected problem; Project illustrates planning design.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Completion evidence can orient a locally supported course-access or counseling inquiry, not automatically prescribe a strategy.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Develop actual strategies, application steps and supporting evidence; Epsilon workshop is a fictional model.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-16\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: planning and refining a response</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q1\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 local evidence checklist; 030 MARKDOWN 16-18; 044 workshop/action-plan development</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-c-2\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part C | planning scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q2\">C.2</a>: Explain how your potential strategies address the equity gap described in your problem statement.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Retain the chosen population and exact outcome; connect each proposed action to supported local conditions.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Distinguish an action&#x27;s intended contribution to EL completion from claims the action has already raised the 70.8% rate.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Explain a plausible evidence-supported relationship and its limits; no intervention evaluation supplied.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-17\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: planning and refining a response</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q2\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 TABLE 23 and synthesis; 030 MARKDOWN 17-18; 040 theory-to-design connection; 043</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-c-3\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part C | planning scaffolding</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q3\">C.3</a>: Explain how your potential strategies for improvement address or take into account the potential contributing factors, including institutional and/or structural factors, and how they align with the school&#x27;s vision, mission, and/or goals.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Use the outcome-to-conditions sequence, local priorities and framework alignment model.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> LEA Met status does not remove possible local access barriers or demonstrate mission alignment.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Use actual school goals and local factor findings to justify each strategy.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-18\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: planning and refining a response</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q3\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 Local Conditions; 030 MARKDOWN 18; 040,044</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-c-4\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part C | requirement reminder only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q4\">C.4</a>: Describe the targeted feedback you received on each proposed strategy from your administrator, supervisor, or other key educational leader(s), and explain how you would adjust your proposed strategies to address the needs of the student group and inform equitable school improvement based on that feedback.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Support page explains the need for educational leader feedback and revision; Project gives an illustrative review cycle.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> There is no actual Jordan leader feedback in the public-data app.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Gather and document targeted feedback on each proposal and explain corresponding revisions.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-18\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: planning and refining a response</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q4\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>030 MARKDOWN 18,32; 044 sections 9-11</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-c-5\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part C | planning/context support</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q5\">C.5</a>: Describe steps you would take to create school-level and community educational partner buy-in to the final adjusted set of proposed strategies. What potential implications for proposed strategies do you anticipate encountering as you address the equity gap at the school?</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Language context can inform accessible outreach; framework community engagement concepts and support prompts help plan participation.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> 2025-26 language-source context reports 120 EL students with Spanish; Castilian. It does not establish all family language preferences or consent.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Plan authentic engagement, implications, resources and revisions with locally verified access needs; do not claim buy-in occurred.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-18\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: planning and refining a response</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/c-q5\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 English Learner languages and Priority 3; 030 MARKDOWN 18,32; 040,044</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-d-1\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part D | reflection prompt only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q1\">D.1</a>: Provide your rationale for the administrator, supervisor, or educational leader feedback you chose to gather in Step 3 and how the feedback impacted your approach to building positive educational partner buy-in.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Support page identifies reflection on feedback-provider selection and its effect on buy-in.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> No public Jordan record documents the candidate&#x27;s leader selection or feedback.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Explain actual selection rationale and feedback&#x27;s effect with evidence from Step 3.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-19\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: reflecting on leadership learning</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q1\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>030 MARKDOWN 19-21,32</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-d-2\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part D | evidence organization plus reflection guidance</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q2\">D.2</a>: Reflect on what you have learned, including strengths and areas for growth as an equity-driven leader. Then discuss and refer to evidence from Steps 1, 2, and/or 3 as to how you addressed equity needs and equity gaps for the identified group of students at your school.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Saved figures, sources and exports can support an evidence trail about disciplined interpretation and inquiry; tutorials offer ethical/non-deficit reflection lenses.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Recognizing that 70.8% is an accountability outcome rather than a causal explanation may inform reflection, but is not evidence of completed action.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Reflect on own learning and actual Steps 1-3 evidence; do not claim the app or a proposed strategy closed the gap.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-19\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: reflecting on leadership learning</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q2\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>010 verification and guardrails; 030 MARKDOWN 19-21; 040; 060</p></details></section><section class=\"question\" id=\"help-d-3\"><p class=\"eyebrow\">Part D | reflection prompt only</p><h3><a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q3\">D.3</a>: Based on the analysis of your experiences in Cycle 1, identify specific professional learning goals for yourself and describe future steps for your professional growth.</h3><p><strong>Where the app helps:</strong> Support and framework pages identify skills worth considering: source verification, qualitative inquiry, research alignment, community engagement and bounded claims.</p><p><strong>Jordan example or application:</strong> Data literacy or multilingual engagement may be possible areas to consider, not app-determined candidate deficits.</p><p><strong>What you still need:</strong> Choose specific goals from personal Cycle 1 experience, with concrete future steps.</p><p><a href=\"#source/support/explanation-19\">Saved Cycle 1 Support: reflecting on leadership learning</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c1/d-q3\">Worked example and rubric context</a>.</p><details><summary>Source record for this connection</summary><p>030 MARKDOWN 19-21; 040-044</p></details></section><h3>Part A II: the qualitative evidence table</h3><p>The table is essential even though it is not another numbered question in the twenty-question map. Record and analyze at least three different qualitative sources from your real setting. Public aggregate tables, three app charts, and three exports of the same data do not supply those sources. Explain recurring findings, differences, and counterexamples, and connect them to the quantitative pattern and school commitments.</p></section><section id=\"framework\"><h2>Archived Framework tutorials: useful reasoning, not a current navigation promise</h2><p>The October 6 app included a Theoretical and Conceptual Framework destination. Current local source removed that destination from navigation on October 7. The screenshots and saved texts below document the older tutorial; they do not establish that these controls are available in the live app today.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"Archived Framework tutorial selector\" aria-label=\"Enlarge Archived Framework tutorial selector\" title=\"Enlarge Archived Framework tutorial selector\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/framework.png\" alt=\"Archived Framework tutorial selector\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Historical selector with Overview, Elementary School, Middle School, High School, and Project. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Historical selector</th><th scope=\"col\">What its tutorial explains</th><th scope=\"col\">Saved reading</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Historical selector\">Overview</td><td data-label=\"What its tutorial explains\">Theory versus conceptual framework; Community Cultural Wealth, culturally responsive leadership, Funds of Knowledge, ethical data stewardship, improvement science; six-question evidence-to-action model.</td><td data-label=\"Saved reading\"><a href=\"sources/040_framework_overview_rendered.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open archived Overview tutorial</a></td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Historical selector\">Elementary School</td><td data-label=\"What its tutorial explains\">Fictional Epsilon qualitative attendance-process thesis: theoretical sensitizing concepts, recruitment, episode interviews/observations/documents, iterative coding and theoretical sampling, ethical protection.</td><td data-label=\"Saved reading\"><a href=\"sources/041_framework_elementary_rendered.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open archived Elementary School tutorial</a></td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Historical selector\">Middle School</td><td data-label=\"What its tutorial explains\">Fictional Epsilon quantitative observational attendance/belonging thesis: questions/hypotheses, measurement, time windows, sampling, estimand/model, uncertainty and missing data; aggregate app rows cannot support individual-level analysis.</td><td data-label=\"Saved reading\"><a href=\"sources/042_framework_middle_rendered.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open archived Middle School tutorial</a></td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Historical selector\">High School</td><td data-label=\"What its tutorial explains\">Fictional Epsilon convergent mixed-methods mathematics-support thesis: availability/accessibility/usability, separate strands, joint displays, convergence/complementarity/discordance/silence, bounded integrated claims.</td><td data-label=\"Saved reading\"><a href=\"sources/043_framework_high_rendered.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open archived High School tutorial</a></td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Historical selector\">Project</td><td data-label=\"What its tutorial explains\">Fictional district administrator professional-development product: needs assessment, workshop cases, facilitation tools, feedback/pilot/revisions and evaluation; no actual effectiveness established.</td><td data-label=\"Saved reading\"><a href=\"sources/044_framework_project_rendered.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Open archived Project tutorial</a></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The historical PDF/Word controls download the selected tutorial, not a Jordan school report. Overview introduces theory and conceptual organization; each school-level or Project choice has its own tutorial and export. All Epsilon examples are fictional. They may help you frame questions about resources, access, usability, and outcomes, but they are not your local qualitative evidence or a required CalAPA research design.</p><p>A theoretical framework offers ideas for interpreting a problem. A conceptual framework identifies the relationships you propose to examine in this inquiry. Either can help you make assumptions visible; neither turns an assumption into a verified cause. Read the underlying scholarship and explain its fit and limitations before applying it in Parts B or C.</p></section><section id=\"verification\"><h2>Sources, verification, and downloads: keep the claim traceable</h2><p>The app's academic sections include the external link <strong>Verify this school, subject and year in official CAASPP results</strong>. It opens an official report for a particular school, subject, and year. It is not a universal in-app verification button for every measure. Check the selected identity, year, grade, group, counts, and measure when using the official destination.</p><p>The inspected local app source checks retained academic records against their source fields and builds verification tables into academic report exports. Those checks are useful, but a saved match is not a fresh check of the latest official release. This revision did not generate or validate new live PDF/Word exports.</p><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Before using a figure</th><th scope=\"col\">Jordan example</th><th scope=\"col\">Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Identity and period</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">CDS 19647331934454; reporting 2025 or academic 2024-25 as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Capture date October 2026 is not outcome year 2026.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Measure and population</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">Math: 121 valid scores; attendance: 875 eligible; suspension: 940 cumulative enrollment.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Denominators answer different questions and cannot be exchanged.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Source definition</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">Graduation includes a qualified fifth-year contribution; ELPI has accountability participation rules.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Similar labels do not establish identical historical definitions.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Missing or suppressed information</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">Older academic numerators and some attendance comparator source metadata are unavailable in retained views.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Leave unavailable values unavailable. Do not infer suppressed counts or call missing source proof complete.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Comparison and precision</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">EL graduation minus inclusive schoolwide is -15.1 percentage points; ELA combined result is 55.28%.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Do not add overlapping subgroups, sum rounded components to replace a source value, or mistake a descriptive gap for a significance test.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Before using a figure\">Claim and next evidence</td><td data-label=\"Jordan example\">A reported outcome difference leads to a question about opportunity and support.</td><td data-label=\"Why it matters\">Public aggregates do not identify causes, individual students across measures, or an intervention effect.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>For each figure, retain the source file or archive, school identifier, measure, year, group, numerator where reported, denominator, rate, and qualification. Check the actual download for readable tables and the same selection you intended. A screenshot helps orient you; the detailed source record supports the claim.</p><h3>About This Project</h3><p>About explains the app's purpose, authorship, and limits of preliminary public evidence and professional judgment. Its PDF and Word controls export that explanatory page. The author's account is not your Part D reflection or evidence about school practice.</p><figure class=\"c1-figure\"><button class=\"c1-image-expand\" type=\"button\" data-figure-expand data-image-title=\"About This Project\" aria-label=\"Enlarge About This Project\" title=\"Enlarge About This Project\"><img src=\"assets/gap-app-pages/about.png\" alt=\"About This Project\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"1440\" height=\"1080\"><span class=\"map-expand-icon\"><i data-lucide=\"expand\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></span></button><figcaption>Purpose, authorship, and professional-judgment boundaries. Saved October 6, 2026 view; not a live connection.</figcaption></figure><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Control in the saved app</th><th scope=\"col\">What it does</th><th scope=\"col\">What appears or is retained</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download About This Project (PDF)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the project purpose, authorship, and limitations. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Control in the saved app\">Download About This Project (Word)</td><td data-label=\"What it does\">Downloads a PDF or Word document, as labeled.</td><td data-label=\"What appears or is retained\">Contains the project purpose, authorship, and limitations. Check the downloaded file before using it.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p><a href=\"sources/060_about_this_project.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Read the saved source text and tables</a> &middot; <a href=\"sources/equity-help-public-evidence.json\" download>Jordan evidence used on this page</a></p></section><section id=\"chapter-one\"><h2>If you are also writing a graduate Chapter One</h2><p>Use the app to establish a bounded public context and a documented outcome pattern, then explain what is still unknown. A Chapter One problem statement may distinguish the observed disparity from the local processes that require investigation. Your purpose and questions should follow that distinction, with the design and ethical approvals required by your program.</p><div class=\"c1-table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th scope=\"col\">Chapter One component</th><th scope=\"col\">Useful app material</th><th scope=\"col\">Your intellectual work</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td data-label=\"Chapter One component\">Context and background</td><td data-label=\"Useful app material\">Verified school identity, Full Report, local conditions, source periods.</td><td data-label=\"Your intellectual work\">Explain the setting and scope without treating district reporting status as a school-level finding.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Chapter One component\">Problem evidence</td><td data-label=\"Useful app material\">Qualified outcome tables, subgroup comparisons, three-year patterns.</td><td data-label=\"Your intellectual work\">Define the measure and disparity; do not invent a causal explanation.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Chapter One component\">Purpose and questions</td><td data-label=\"Useful app material\">Cycle 1 Support inquiry prompts; archived framework examples if appropriate.</td><td data-label=\"Your intellectual work\">State what your own study or project will examine and why new evidence is needed.</td></tr><tr><td data-label=\"Chapter One component\">Significance, scope, limitations</td><td data-label=\"Useful app material\">Counts, source coverage, missing data, comparability notes.</td><td data-label=\"Your intellectual work\">Explain who may benefit, what the evidence can support, and what remains outside the inquiry.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>A defensible Jordan starting point is that the reported English Learner graduation rate remains below schoolwide in the saved 2023-2025 series, with source-definition qualifications. That motivates questions about relevant opportunities and support; it does not establish that a particular Jordan practice caused the difference. The exact chapter structure comes from your graduate program. CalAPA Cycle 1 instead uses its four required Parts A-D.</p><p><a href=\"#cycle/c1/part-a\">Return to Cycle 1 Part A</a> &middot; <a href=\"#cycle/c2\">Continue to Cycle 2</a></p></section></article>"};
